        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): keep CDP cursor text previews UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`findCursorInteractiveElements` truncates DOM text in a **browser** `Runtime.evaluate` page expression with `.slice(0, 101)`. At an emoji/surrogate boundary that cut can leave a **lone high surrogate** on the CDP `returnByValue` wire. Node `truncateUtf16Safe(..., 100)` cannot repair a lone surrogate when the string is already `length === 100` (no-op). Approaches that *call* Node/SDK `truncateUtf16Safe` **inside** the page expression throw `ReferenceError` and fail closed to an empty cursor map (the previous tip of this PR, and the failure mode of that shape).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOwn the cut in a **page-local**, dependency-free helper (`truncateCdpPageTextPreview`) injected via `Function#toString`, and unify the page/Node preview budget at **100**. Node still re-applies the same cap as defense for odd evaluate payloads.\n\n**Vs [#108316](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/108316):** same correct seam (page-injectable truncate — not Node-in-page). This PR keeps it to **2 files** (`cdp.ts` + `cdp.test.ts`) instead of adding a third module + test file, keeps the `\\s` whitespace normalization from main (no incidental regex drift), and uses a leaner 3-case unit suite focused on the wire hole + injectability contract.\n\nNon-goals: no live Chrome CDP redesign; do not inject `truncateUtf16Safe.toString()` alone (closes over `sliceUtf16Safe` / surrogate helpers).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Before:** Unsafe page `.slice` can put a lone surrogate on the evaluate payload; Node re-truncate at the final budget may leave it. Node-helper-in-page calls empty the cursor-interactive map.\n- **After:** Page preview truncate is UTF-16 safe before `returnByValue`; Node re-cap stays defense-in-depth; page expression does not call Node/SDK helpers.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Head SHA:** `2247ff560ce21e233b7c59109d35f73a56c6f7dd`\n**Base:** `55a822dc6877afd588dda6e8d17e64ba360041b5`\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Page helper at 100-unit emoji boundary | drops whole emoji; no lone surrogate |\n| Unsafe `.slice(0,100)` + Node `truncateUtf16Safe(...,100)` | lone surrogate survives (documents the hole) |\n| Injected expression via `Function#toString` | embeds page helper; does **not** call `truncateUtf16Safe(` |\n| Smoke (local node) | `previewLone: false`, `nodeStillLone: true` on same fixture |\n\nFocused tests live in `extensions/browser/src/browser/cdp.test.ts` (`truncateCdpPageTextPreview`).\n\n## Review\n\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
